(3001490, 420185, 41574, '<td valign="top">I guess you submitted this to the wrong challenge; sorry.</td>', 'I guess you submitted this to the wrong challenge; sorry.', '2006-11-05 11:51:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(3001491, 418382, 41574, '<td valign="top">Great.</td>', 'Great.', '2006-11-05 11:51:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(3001492, 419948, 41574, '<td valign="top">I guess you submitted this to the wrong challenge.</td>', 'I guess you submitted this to the wrong challenge.', '2006-11-05 11:52:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(3001496, 419790, 41574, '<td valign="top">It''s clever, and I think it works; but your depth of field doesn''t seem to quite extend to infinity, and that hurts your shot.</td>', 'It''s clever, and I think it works; but your depth of field doesn''t seem to quite extend to infinity, and that hurts your shot.', '2006-11-05 11:53:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(3001507, 420509, 60281, '<td valign="top">This is the only image in the challenge that I dont feel I have seen before.  It shows creativity and lateral thinking. It offers a perspective of the world filled with emotion and devoid of complication. It fits its title with superb craft and is well executed too.</td>', 'This is the only image in the challenge that I dont feel I have seen before.  It shows creativity and lateral thinking. It offers a perspective of the world filled with emotion and devoid of complication. It fits its title with superb craft and is well executed too.', '2006-11-05 12:01:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(3001532, 419432, 60281, '<td valign="top">What a shame it is so small! It look like an interesting composition with gentle tones but its so small I cant really tell.</td>', 'What a shame it is so small! It look like an interesting composition with gentle tones but its so small I cant really tell.', '2006-11-05 12:09:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(3001533, 419294, 60281, '<td valign="top">Nice tones and an reasonable composition. It looks to be blurred due to camera shake though. The grainy (noisy) texture suggests that this was a long exposure and a tripod or other convenient support would have helped to eliminate the camera shake. Sometimes with longer exposures and the chance of camera shake it is a good idea to take several identical pictures and pick the sharpest one later.</td>', 'Nice tones and an reasonable composition. It looks to be blurred due to camera shake though. The grainy (noisy) texture suggests that this was a long exposure and a tripod or other convenient support would have helped to eliminate the camera shake. Sometimes with longer exposures and the chance of camera shake it is a good idea to take several identical pictures and pick the sharpest one later.', '2006-11-05 12:09:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(3001547, 418471, 60805, '<td valign="top">ANNNNNNNNNNNND it''s a 10 lol</td>', 'ANNNNNNNNNNNND it''s a 10 lol', '2006-11-05 12:13:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(3001553, 417083, 60281, '<td valign="top">The image is rather small and dark and Im afraid I just cant figure out what is going on. It seems it could possible be an interesting picture but its just too dark to tell for sure.</td>', 'The image is rather small and dark and Im afraid I just cant figure out what is going on. It seems it could possible be an interesting picture but its just too dark to tell for sure.', '2006-11-05 12:14:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(3001601, 420491, 60281, '<td valign="top">The reflections of the windows on the opposite side of the train (Im assuming train) have spoilt this picture. You need to get the lens as close a possible to glass when photographing through it to avoid reflections like these. I find it best to place one hand on the glass and press the camera firmly against my fingers so as to avoid contacting the lens with the window, yet still getting it very close.<br/>Other than the above, you did very well to get this image from a moving train. It is a nice composition and I would like to see what you could have achieved if you had be able to get out and take your time.</td>', 'The reflections of the windows on the opposite side of the train (Im assuming train) have spoilt this picture. You need to get the lens as close a possible to glass when photographing through it to avoid reflections like these. I find it best to place one hand on the glass and press the camera firmly against my fingers so as to avoid contacting the lens with the window, yet still getting it very close.Other than the above, you did very well to get this image from a moving train. It is a nice composition and I would like to see what you could have achieved if you had be able to get out and take your time.', '2006-11-05 12:23:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(3001612, 420806, 60281, '<td valign="top">Had the focus been on the town I feel this would have worked mush better. As it is my eyes are drawn and held on the crest of the foreground, which sadly has little interest.</td>', 'Had the focus been on the town I feel this would have worked mush better. As it is my eyes are drawn and held on the crest of the foreground, which sadly has little interest.', '2006-11-05 12:25:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(3001622, 419268, 60281, '<td valign="top">This seems to be an interesting picture, with leading lines and the complementary colour of the lines down the road. However the picture is just to small to be able to judge it properly :-(</td>', 'This seems to be an interesting picture, with leading lines and the complementary colour of the lines down the road. However the picture is just to small to be able to judge it properly :-(', '2006-11-05 12:27:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(3001642, 418297, 60281, '<td valign="top">A very bold and confident crop, I like the unusual and that is what you have gone for. Unfortunately I dont think the foreground has enough interest to work with this move. I would try more of this extreme cropping, as it has potential, but I think you need to experiment with the foreground to make it work.</td>', 'A very bold and confident crop, I like the unusual and that is what you have gone for. Unfortunately I dont think the foreground has enough interest to work with this move. I would try more of this extreme cropping, as it has potential, but I think you need to experiment with the foreground to make it work.', '2006-11-05 12:32:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(3001696, 418797, 60281, '<td valign="top">A sharp and well exposed image with good colours. I find it a rather cluttered composition however. It doesnt have any focal point and although the far side of the lock acts as a leading line it is somewhat lost in the clutter and doesnt lead my eye to anything particularly interesting. The technical side is good you just need to work on the composition :-)</td>', 'A sharp and well exposed image with good colours. I find it a rather cluttered composition however. It doesnt have any focal point and although the far side of the lock acts as a leading line it is somewhat lost in the clutter and doesnt lead my eye to anything particularly interesting. The technical side is good you just need to work on the composition :-)', '2006-11-05 12:44:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(3001723, 417790, 60281, '<td valign="top">This seems to be rather over-exposed, which is a shame as it is a good picture otherwise. Im not sure about the drop-shadow border. While they can look great in some circumstances, such as catalogues, I dont think they work so well for a stand-alone picture  they tend to be distracting rather than enhancing.</td>', 'This seems to be rather over-exposed, which is a shame as it is a good picture otherwise. Im not sure about the drop-shadow border. While they can look great in some circumstances, such as catalogues, I dont think they work so well for a stand-alone picture  they tend to be distracting rather than enhancing.', '2006-11-05 12:50:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(3001733, 417722, 60281, '<td valign="top">This looks a touch over sharpened, the halos around the tower structure are somewhat distracting. I would try a smaller radius for the USM.</td>', 'This looks a touch over sharpened, the halos around the tower structure are somewhat distracting. I would try a smaller radius for the USM.', '2006-11-05 12:53:14.000000', NULL, 1),
