(3015545, 418315, 44099, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments everyone! Another high-scorer for me, but still haven''t broken 6 yet. Anyway, thank God for advanced editing, in fact a lot of editing went into this image to get all the colors and WB right...<br/> <br/>You guys are right about the shadow though...originally the image had a very large shadow in the bottom-right corner and I had cropped out a lot of it for this, but didn''t get rid of it completely. I''ll have to watch the composition before shooting next time.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments everyone! Another high-scorer for me, but still haven''t broken 6 yet. Anyway, thank God for advanced editing, in fact a lot of editing went into this image to get all the colors and WB right... You guys are right about the shadow though...originally the image had a very large shadow in the bottom-right corner and I had cropped out a lot of it for this, but didn''t get rid of it completely. I''ll have to watch the composition before shooting next time.', '2006-11-08 17:38:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(3015683, 419336, 59215, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by elizadeb:</b></div><hr/><i> My Landscape entry into this challenge was also taken at Lake Powell!  Isn''t it a beautiful place?!  I took a gazillion photos and couldn''t decide which one to enter.  I selected an unusual view....through a pueblo window....it finished above ''6'' so I''m happy!  But you always wonder "what IF I would have entered the other one...!)  Great Job! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ha! I completely understand... This photo is a personal best so I''m excited about that, but it is very tempting to wonder "what if?" hehe! <br/> <br/>Lake Powell is an amazing place...<br/> <br/>Congrats on your above ''6'' picture too, the framing is very cool!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by elizadeb: My Landscape entry into this challenge was also taken at Lake Powell!  Isn''t it a beautiful place?!  I took a gazillion photos and couldn''t decide which one to enter.  I selected an unusual view....through a pueblo window....it finished above ''6'' so I''m happy!  But you always wonder "what IF I would have entered the other one...!)  Great Job!   Ha! I completely understand... This photo is a personal best so I''m excited about that, but it is very tempting to wonder "what if?" hehe!  Lake Powell is an amazing place... Congrats on your above ''6'' picture too, the framing is very cool! ', '2006-11-08 18:33:54.000000', NULL, 0),
