(3018215, 417350, 25095, '<td valign="top">you are right, it is a good photo...without the frame.  I like the way you siloutted (I can''t spell) the foreground and those clouds are beautiful.  At first I thought it was looking over some berms at a beach and those were waves crashing in the background, but now I see it is mostly sky.  <br/> <br/>If I might suggest some improvements (depending of course on your software choices of course)...in Adobe Photoshop if you go into selective color you can adjust each color on different levels at a time, I have found this is really helpful to get blacks really black and whites really white.  It can help with some dull colors too.  If you have access to adobe or something like it you may want to check in to that.<br/> <br/>If you have other questions I am by far not an expert but would be happy to help, pm me.</td>', 'you are right, it is a good photo...without the frame.  I like the way you siloutted (I can''t spell) the foreground and those clouds are beautiful.  At first I thought it was looking over some berms at a beach and those were waves crashing in the background, but now I see it is mostly sky.   If I might suggest some improvements (depending of course on your software choices of course)...in Adobe Photoshop if you go into selective color you can adjust each color on different levels at a time, I have found this is really helpful to get blacks really black and whites really white.  It can help with some dull colors too.  If you have access to adobe or something like it you may want to check in to that. If you have other questions I am by far not an expert but would be happy to help, pm me.', '2006-11-09 16:32:31.000000', NULL, 0),
