(3023989, 417472, 36060, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by MPRPRO:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Structor:</b></div><hr/><i> Congratulations on your top 10 finish. This is a great shot of bridge, but where are the Landscape? </i></td></tr></table>Obviously someone saw one otherwise I don''t think it would have scored so high. But seriously folks, there is land on the other side of the river. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Please don´t take me wrong, I like your picture very much, and I think most of the people do also, that is the reason it scored so high. What amazed me is that people are voting on the pictures without taking a note of the challenge. That is my opinion that your picture is  on the edge of the challenge, the main subject is a bridge over a river, and on the other side of the river is a city, not a landscape.</td>', 'Originally posted by MPRPRO: Originally posted by Structor: Congratulations on your top 10 finish. This is a great shot of bridge, but where are the Landscape? Obviously someone saw one otherwise I don''t think it would have scored so high. But seriously folks, there is land on the other side of the river.  Please don´t take me wrong, I like your picture very much, and I think most of the people do also, that is the reason it scored so high. What amazed me is that people are voting on the pictures without taking a note of the challenge. That is my opinion that your picture is  on the edge of the challenge, the main subject is a bridge over a river, and on the other side of the river is a city, not a landscape.', '2006-11-12 15:01:45.000000', NULL, 0),
